URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/twelfth-night-pantaloons/
SUMMARY:TWELFTH NIGHT (Pantaloons)
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: Adult £15\, Friend of the Regal\, Student\, ES40 £13
 .50\n\nThe Pantaloons present\n\nTWELFTH NIGHT\n\nGet in a fight.   Cros
 s-dress.   Throw on some yellow stockings.   Love can make you do the f
 unniest things ...!   The critically-acclaimed Pantaloons Theatre Compan
 y present their own brand of Shakespearean mayhem.\n\nSeparated at sea\, t
 wins Viola and Sebastian wash up on the island of Illyria\, both fearing t
 he other lost forever.   Plied pranksters\, puritanical pillocks and per
 haps even true love await them as they forge their own paths through this 
 new world of fools\, jewels\, duels and dual-identities.\n\nFamily-friendl
 y fun with live music and audience participation!
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/pa
 ntaloons.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1090@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261006T193000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261006T193000
DTSTAMP:20260822T171153Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/romeria-cert-15/
SUMMARY:ROMERÍA (CERT 15)
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: £6 (£4 Regal Film Society member/Student/ES40) \nRo
 mería (Cert 15) \nDir Carla Simón          Spain/Germany 2025
          111 mins\nSpanish director Carla Simón's honest\, open 
 and direct film-making is on show again in Romería\, addressing similar 
 themes to her beautifully observed 2017 film Summer 1993\, which was also
  screened by the film society.\nA young woman arrives in Galicia to find o
 ut about the family she never knew. Orphaned since childhood\, she meets h
 er grandparents\, uncles\, aunts and cousins\, a biological family of whic
 h Marina knows almost nothing.  In the course of the revelations about u
 nspoken events of the past\, Romería explores the traces left by a genera
 tion marked by tragedy and taboo.  Subtitled.\n[embed]https://www.youtub
 e.com/watch?v=da3CAnPA_EM[/embed]\nTrailer: www.youtube.com/watch?v=da3CAn
 PA_EM\nThe Guardian review: www.theguardian.com/film/2025/may/22/romeria-r
 eview-carla-simons-gripping-pilgrimage-tackles-aids-parents-and-the-legacy
 -of-secrets
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/Ro
 meria06.10.26.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1116@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261008T193000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261008T193000
DTSTAMP:20260916T190101Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/drops-making-waves-through-the-arts-pr
 esents-bloomin-church/
SUMMARY:DROPS- PRESENTS BLOOMIN' CHURCH!
DESCRIPTION:Tickets: Adult £12.50\, Regal Friends £11\, Student/ES40 £9.
 50\n\nDROPS- Making Waves through the Arts- presents 'Bloomin' Church'\n\n
 Join the Rev. Dan Fisher and his congregation in this hilarious\, heart-wr
 enching new play as they strive to become a truly ‘Bloomin’ Church!’
 \n\nWith real-life stories\, poetry\, and song\, this uplifting show crack
 s open the walls of “church\,” revealing the mess\, the beauty\, and t
 he surprising potential to bloom when we’re brave enough to be ourselves
 .\n\nHilarious\, honest\, and bursting with song!\n\nPerformance: approx. 
 70mins Followed by: a safe\, open Q&amp\;A / conversation about church\, s
 pirituality\, and living life to the full.\n\n&nbsp\;
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/Bl
 oomin-Church-DROPS.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1119@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261013T193000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261013T193000
DTSTAMP:20260919T090313Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/exhibition-on-screen-david-hockney-at-
 the-royal-academy-of-arts/
SUMMARY:EXHIBITION ON SCREEN: DAVID HOCKNEY AT THE ROYAL ACADEMY OF ARTS
DESCRIPTION:ALL TICKETS £12\n***A special screening to celebrate the life 
 of David Hockney who died earlier this year***\nExhibition on Screen\nDAVI
 D HOCKNEY AT THE ROYAL ACADEMY OF ARTS\nDirected by Phil Grabsky     
      85 mins\nTo celebrate the life of exceptional artist David Hockn
 ey\, Exhibition on Screen's 2017 film is returning to UK cinemas for a lim
 ited run.\nWidely considered Britain's most popular artist\, David Hockney
  is a global sensation with exhibitions in London\, New York\, Paris and b
 eyond\, attracting millions of visitors worldwide.\nFeaturing intimate and
  in-depth interviews with Hockney\, this revealing film focuses on two blo
 ckbuster exhibitions held in 2012 and 2016 at the Royal Academy of Art in 
 London.\nDirector Phil Grabsky secured privileged access to craft this cin
 ematic celebration of a 21st century master of creativity.\n[embed]https:/
 /www.youtube.com/watch?v=rhGeDhpDxOY[/embed]\nTrailer: www.youtube.com/wat
 ch?v=rhGeDhpDxOY
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/EO
 SDavidHockney13.10.26DavidHockneyLA2016©David-Hockney-Photo-Credit-Jean-P
 ierre-Goncalves-de-Lima.webp
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1106@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261022T193000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261024T193000
DTSTAMP:20260825T205408Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/fleet-street/
SUMMARY:FLEET STREET
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: Adults £10.00\, Regal Friends £9.00\, Students £5.0
 0\n\n&nbsp\;\n\nIt’s 1986\, and Printers’ Court is a retirement home f
 or ex-journalists situated down an alley off the main thoroughfare of Flee
 t Street. William Baxter is just recovering from the flu and has left his 
 room for the first time in a fortnight to have breakfast in the dining roo
 m. He is surprised to be joined at his table by Ruby Henderson\, a twice m
 arried ex-journalist who remembers him from their days together at The Lon
 don Globe\, during the war.\n\n&nbsp\;\n\nBack in 1941\, William was known
  as Billy and was an eager cub-reporter\, itching for a scoop. Billy is no
 t\, however\, as desperate for a scoop as Ruby. There’s a killer on the 
 loose\, preying on the vulnerable ladies of Soho under the cover of the Lo
 ndon Blitz\, and “Fleet Street” flips back and forth between 1941 and 
 1986 to piece together the story of his unmasking\, culminating in the awf
 ul night that The Cafe de Paris was bombed in the heart of Piccadilly.\n\n
 &nbsp\;\n\nA whodunit and a story of lost love.\n\n&nbsp\;\n\nA Waterfront
  Theatre production\n\nWritten by Fred Owen\n\n&nbsp\;\n\n&nbsp\;
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/Fl
 eet_Street_image_210826.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1086@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261025T190000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261025T190000
DTSTAMP:20260629T112216Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/wonders-of-our-universe/
SUMMARY:WONDERS OF OUR UNIVERSE
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: Adult £20\, Child (11-16 years) £18\, Regal Friends/
 Student/ES40 £18\, Family ticket (two adults and two children) £70\n\nPl
 ease note start time\n\nThe Average Scientist presents... Wonders of Our U
 niverse\n\nThis isn’t just a theatre show — it’s a voyage through sp
 ace and time like no other.\n\nGuided by astrophysicist Ian Hall FRAS\, yo
 u’ll journey from the explosive birth of the cosmos to humanity’s firs
 t steps beyond Earth\, uncovering the mysteries of black holes\, the vast 
 beauty of distant galaxies\, and the tantalising question of whether we ar
 e alone. With breath-taking visuals and a soaring cinematic soundtrack\, e
 ach moment is crafted to ignite your curiosity and stir your emotions.\n\n
 Visually spectacular\, scientifically rich\, and endlessly inspiring\, Won
 ders of Our Universe will change the way you see the night sky — and you
 r place within it.\n\nThis is science as you’ve never experienced it bef
 ore: live\, cinematic\, and utterly unforgettable.\n\nRecommended Age Guid
 ance: 11 years plus\, although children younger than this will enjoy the s
 how if they are particularly engaged with the topic.\n\n[embed]https://www
 .youtube.com/watch?v=sA4e10H0s6M&t=8s[/embed]\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/ti
 tle_artwork.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1096@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261027T191500
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261027T191500
DTSTAMP:20260825T000135Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/rbo-manon/
SUMMARY:ROYAL BALLET & OPERA: MANON
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: £15.50\, Film Society members/Regal Theatre Friends 
 £14.00\, Students/ES40s £13\, under 14s £10.\n\nPlease note start time\
 n\nThe Royal Ballet LIVE from the Royal Opera House\n\nMANON [Revival]\n\n
 In the seedy underbelly of 18th-century Paris\, money is king.  Nothing i
 s sacred – even love itself can be bought for the right price.  A nativ
 e of this hedonistic underworld\, Manon is caught between twin desires whe
 n she falls in love with the student Des Grieux. Steadfast and devoted\, h
 e offers the possibility of an honourable life.  Yet\, the riches promise
 d by the world of Parisian society remain tempting...\n\nManon’s inner t
 urmoil and struggle for survival lie at the devastating heart of Kenneth M
 acMillan’s 1974 adaptation of Abbé Prévost’s novel.  In this signat
 ure work of The Royal Ballet\, MacMillan’s nuanced understanding of huma
 n psychology makes for an unflinching look into the moral degradation of M
 anon’s Paris\, while all its decadence and decay are brought to life thr
 ough Jules Massenet’s score and Nicholas Georgiadis’s designs.\n\nAppr
 oximate runtime is 190min\, including two Intervals
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/RB
 OManon27.10.26jpeg-copy.jpeg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1083@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261030T193000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261030T193000
DTSTAMP:20260817T185803Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/the-carpenters-experience-2026/
SUMMARY:THE CARPENTERS EXPERIENCE
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: Adults £22.50\, Friends/Students/ES40s £20.00 \n\nT
 he Carpenters Experience \n\nWhen we were young\, we’d listen to the ra
 dio\, waiting for our favourite songs. Now they’re back again\, like a 
 long-lost friend\, all the song’ we loved so well...\n\nThe UK’s leadi
 ng Carpenters show\, featuring the amazing voice of Maggie Nestor and eigh
 t top-class musicians\, captures the sights and sounds of the amazing tale
 nts of Richard and Karen Carpenter.\n\nKaren’s silky contralto is combin
 ed with Richard’s delightful piano and seamless harmonies in this big pr
 oduction that brings Close to You\, We’ve only Just Begun\, Top of the 
 World\, Rainy Days and Mondays\, Solitaire\, Goodbye to Love\, Please Mr P
 ostman\, For All We Know\, Only Yesterday and dozens more classic songs t
 o the stage.\n\nThe Carpenters Experience is coming to town for an evening
  of non-stop hits – it’s yesterday once more...
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/ca
 rpenters-3.jpeg
END:VEVENT
