BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1107@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261103T193000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261103T193000
DTSTAMP:20260826T181828Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/the-summer-book-cert-pg/
SUMMARY:THE SUMMER BOOK (CERT PG)
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: £6 (£4 Regal Film Society member/Student/ES40) \nTh
 e Summer Book (Cert PG)\nDir Charlie McDowell          Finland/
 UK/USA 2024          90 mins\nStarring Glenn Close\, The Summer
  Book follows an intergenerational family spending a transformative summe
 r at their rustic holiday home on an unspoiled\, remote island in the Gulf
  of Finland.\nAdapted from Tove Jansson's beloved novel\, the film explore
 s grief\, nature\, and the delicate bonds between a young girl\, her wise 
 grandmother\, played to perfection by Close\, and her grieving father (And
 ers Danielsen Lie).\n[embed]https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_ZfIALnLZnI[/e
 mbed]\nTrailer: www.youtube.com/watch?v=_ZfIALnLZnI\nThe Observer review:
   observer.co.uk/culture/film/article/the-summer-book-this-tove-jansson-a
 daptation-is-a-masterclass-in-restraint
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/Th
 eSummerBook03.11.26.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1094@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261112T193000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261114T193000
DTSTAMP:20260821T224304Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/abigails-party-by-mike-leigh/
SUMMARY:ABIGAIL'S PARTY BY MIKE LEIGH
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: Adults £11.50\; Regal Friends/Student/Children/ES40 
 £9.50\n\nBarnstormers are proud to present Abigail’s Party\, an iconic 
 tragi-comedy by Mike Leigh. Set in 1977 suburban England Abigail’s Party
  is a sharp\, black comedy that has stood the test of time and remains rel
 evant today.\n\nIt follows controlling hostess Beverly and her stressed hu
 sband Laurence as they host drinks for new neighbours Angela and Tony alon
 gside nervous neighbour Susan\, whose teenage daughter Abigail is throwing
  a loud party next door. The alcohol is flowing\, Demis  Roussos is on th
 e record player\, and cheese and pineapple cocktail sticks are ready to go
 . However\, before long polite small talk turns toxic and simmering marita
 l tensions explode\, leading to a climax that nobody has expected....\n\nD
 irected by the very talented Mary Noble\, a play truly not to be missed.\n
 \nThis amateur production is presented by arrangement with Concord Theatri
 cals Ltd on\n\nbehalf of Samuel French Ltd.www.concordtheatricals.co.uk\n\
 n&nbsp\;
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/ab
 igail-party.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1097@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261115T140000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261115T140000
DTSTAMP:20260825T000251Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/rbo-carmen/
SUMMARY:ROYAL BALLET & OPERA: CARMEN
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: £15.50\, Film Society members/Regal Theatre Friends 
 £14.00\, Students/ES40s £13\, under 14s £10.\n\nPlease note start time\
 n\nThe Royal Opera ENCORE LIVE BROADCAST from the Royal Opera House\n\nCAR
 MEN [Revival]\n\nUnder the oppressive heat of the Spanish sun\, the fierce
 ly independent Carmen attracts the attention of Don José.  She warns him
  not to fall in love with her\, but his obsession knows no bounds. Damiano
  Michieletto’s searing production returns\, casting scorching light on t
 he lust\, violence and destructive desire of Bizet’s ever-popular opera.
 \n\nAn all-star cast brings this white-hot drama to life\, with Ginger Cos
 ta-Jackson in the fiery title role\, alongside Russell Thomas as the jealo
 us and despairing Don José. Following his 2023 Royal Opera debut\, Sesto 
 Quatrini returns to conduct Bizet’s electrifying and sensual score.\n\nS
 ung in French with English subtitles.\n\nApproximate runtime 215min\, incl
 uding one Interval
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/RB
 OCarmen15.11.26-copy.png
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1109@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261126T193000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261128T193000
DTSTAMP:20260905T191449Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/agatha-crusty-and-the-village-hall-mur
 ders/
SUMMARY:AGATHA CRUSTY AND THE VILLAGE HALL MURDERS
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: Adult: £11.50/ Regal Friends: £11.00/  Children\, S
 tudent\, ES40:  £9.50\n\nWhere would a renowned crime writer go for a re
 laxing\, peaceful break away from the murder and intrigue of her novels? W
 hy Chortleby\, of course!!\n\nInvited by her sister-in-law\, Alice\, to sp
 end a few peaceful days enjoying rural village life\, Agatha Crusty (prono
 unced Croosty) soon finds herself using her skills as a crime writer and p
 ast experience of solving crimes as she gets embroiled in a series of murd
 ers.\n\nFrom Toby\, the vicar\, and Eleanor\, Chair of the Village Hall Co
 mmittee\, to Harry Knott\, the caretaker\, and identical twins Olivia and 
 Oliver Truscott-Pratt\, there are plenty of suspects. Add an incompetent i
 nvestigating officer\, DI Twigg\, and the laughs pile up as quickly as the
  bodies.\n\nPacked full of wit and very funny scenes\, this is also a genu
 ine murder mystery which will tax those little grey cells!!\n\nJoin us for
  an evening of sleuthing and giggles\n\n&nbsp\;
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/12
 97.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1098@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261201T191500
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261201T191500
DTSTAMP:20260825T000304Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/rbo-the-nutcracker/
SUMMARY:ROYAL BALLET & OPERA: THE NUTCRACKER
DESCRIPTION:Tickets: £15.50\, Film Society members/Regal Theatre Friends 
 £14.00\, Students/ES40s £13\, under 14s £10.\n\nPlease note start time\
 n\nThe Royal Ballet AS LIVE from the Royal Opera House\n\nTHE NUTCRACKER [
 Revival]\n\nFilmed 10th December 2025\n\nAt a cosy Christmas party\, young
  Clara meets the mysterious magician Drosselmeyer\, who gives her a nutcra
 cker doll.  When the guests have departed and the house is asleep\, Clara
  sneaks downstairs in search of the doll.  Instead\, she finds Drosselmey
 er\, who whisks her away on a journey into a whole world of enchantment: f
 antastical landscapes of flurried snow and glittering confection where toy
 s come alive and the magic never stops.\n\nPeter Wright’s production of 
 this festive family favourite sparkles to the wondrous swell of Tchaikovsk
 y’s orchestral score\, alongside the glow and grandeur of Julia Trevelya
 n Oman’s period designs.\n\nApproximate runtime 140min\, including one I
 nterval
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/RB
 OTheNutcracker01.12.26-copy.jpeg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1120@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261205T193000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261205T193000
DTSTAMP:20260919T204619Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/andre-rieu-2026-christmas-concert-let-
 it-snow/
SUMMARY:ANDRÉ RIEU 2026 CHRISTMAS CONCERT: LET IT SNOW
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: £15.50\; Film Society member/Friend of the Regal £14
 .00\; Student/ES40 £13\; under 14 £10\n\nThis holiday season\, celebrate
  the most wonderful time of the year on the big screen with André Rieu's 
 2026 Christmas Concert – Let It Snow.  This heartwarming festive specta
 cular\, ?lled with beloved Christmas classics\, enchanting waltzes and mag
 ical surprises\, will leave you smiling long after the ?nal encore.\n\nJoi
 ned by his world-famous Johann Strauss Orchestra\, exceptional sopranos an
 d a powerful 120-voice male choir\, André brings the spirit of Christmas 
 to life in an unforgettable musical event.  Over?owing with music\, laugh
 ter and holiday cheer\, this concert is perfect for the whole family.\n\nW
 hether you're surrounded by snow or simply dreaming of it\, experience the
  magic of Christmas on the big screen with those you love.  Wrap up your 
 year with Let It Snow – only in cinemas!\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/An
 dreRieuChristmasConcert2026Pic2.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1088@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261212T143000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261219T193000
DTSTAMP:20260817T190821Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/dick-whittington/
SUMMARY:DICK WHITTINGTON
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: Adult £15\, Children £10\, Family Ticket (2 adults &
 amp\; 2 children) £45.\nSaturday 12th December 2.30pm Matinee\nSaturday 1
 2th December 7.30pm Evening\nSunday    13th December 2.30pm Matinee\nTh
 ursday 17th December 7.30pm Evening\nFriday      18th December 7.30pm E
 vening\nSaturday 19th December 2.30pm Matinee\nSaturday 19th December 7.30
 pm Evening\nMinehead Panto People present...\nDick Whittington\nA brave an
 d ambitious country boy\, travels to London in the belief the streets are 
 ‘paved with gold’\, in this classic rags to riches tale.\nJoined by To
 m\, a cool talking cat\, Dick finds employment at Alderman Fitzwarren’s 
 store.\nWorking alongside the Alderman’s daughter Alice\, Dolly Dumpling
  his cook and her lazy son\, Idle Jack\, Dick quickly falls in love\, but 
 what has the sinister King Rat and his mini Ratlings\, who infest London\,
  got planned for him?\nFollowing a setup\, Dick is forced to return home\,
  but dreaming of Alice and becoming Lord Mayor of London\, he resolves to 
 return and clear his name.\nNot wanting to be seen\, Dick and Tom stow awa
 y on Alderman Fitzwarren’s ship the ‘Billy O’Tea’ as it sets sail 
 with Captain Cuttlefish and his idiotic mate Scupper at the helm.\nSurvivi
 ng a shipwreck\, they are all washed up on the shores of Morocco. Will Dic
 k now triumph over the villainous King Rat and be generously rewarded by t
 he Sultan?\nJoin Minehead Panto People\, as Fairy Bowbells protects and ma
 gically guides Dick to his true destiny. Will he get to be a wealthy man a
 nd marry Alice? Will he become Lord Mayor of London?\n&nbsp\;
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/Di
 ck-Whittington-Banner.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1117@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261221T140000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261221T140000
