URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/the-santa-show-2026-santas-best-ever-c
 hristmas/
SUMMARY:THE SANTA SHOW 2026    SANTA'S BEST EVER CHRISTMAS
DESCRIPTION:Tickets: Adult £10\, Regal Friends/Child £9\, Family Ticket (
 Adults and 2 Children) £34\n\nJoin Father Christmas and friends in this 
 brand new\, festive\, musical\, interactive adventure to make 2026 Santa
 ’s Best Ever Christmas! Featuring the voice of children’s TV star CHRI
 S JARVIS as Dasher the Reindeer\, it’s a family show most suitable for 2
 -8 year olds\, where every child will receive a specially wrapped present 
 from Santa - after the most Christmassy Christmas show ever\, HO-HO-HO!\n\
 nSongs include children’s favourites:\n\nJingle Bells\, The Hokey Cokey\
 , Away In A Manger\, Baby Shark\, The Twelve Days Of Christmas\, We Wish Y
 ou A Merry Christmas\, and many more!\n\n&nbsp\;
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/sa
 ntas-best-ever-xmas.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1099@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20270126T180000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20270126T180000
DTSTAMP:20260825T000637Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/rbo-la-fanciulla-del-west/
SUMMARY:ROYAL BALLET & OPERA: LA FANCIULLA DEL WEST
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: £15.50\, Film Society members/Regal Theatre Friends 
 £14.00\, Students/ES40s £13\, under 14s £10.\n\nPlease note start time\
 n\nThe Metropolitan Opera AS LIVE from the Metropolitan Opera House\, New 
 York\n\nLA FANCIULLA DEL WEST [New Production]\n\nFilmed 23rd January 2027
 \n\nPuccini’s exhilarating drama of the Wild West returns in a new stagi
 ng by celebrated British director Richard Jones\, marking the company’s 
 first new production of La Fanciulla del West in more than 30 years.\n\nSo
 prano Sondra Radvanovsky adds to her already remarkable Met repertoire\, m
 aking her role debut as Minnie\, the tough tavern owner with a heart of go
 ld who finds love when she least expects it. Tenor SeokJong Baek is the da
 shing bandit who rambles into the remote California mining town to steal h
 er heart\, opposite baritone Christopher Maltman as the lawman determined 
 to deliver rough justice—and win Minnie for himself.\n\nMaestro Keri-Lyn
 n Wilson takes the podium to conduct one of opera’s most action-packed a
 dventures\, live from the Met stage to cinemas worldwide.  This productio
 n is part of the Met’s award-winning Live in HD series\, bringing opera 
 to cinemas across the globe.\n\nSung in Italian with English subtitles.\n\
 nApproximate runtime 195min\, including one Interval
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/RB
 OLaFancuillaDelWestd26.01.27-copy.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1112@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20270129T143000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20270130T190000
DTSTAMP:20260912T201155Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/together-we-dance/
SUMMARY:TOGETHER WE DANCE
DESCRIPTION:Tickets: Adult: £10/ Child £6/ Family of 4 £30/ Regal Frien
 ds £8\nFriday\,  29th January at 7:00PM\nSaturday\, 30th January at 2:30
 PM\nImpakt &amp\; Divas and Dudes are proud to present an evening celebrat
 ing dance\, friendship\, confidence\, and inclusion.\n\nOur show brings to
 gether two wonderful performance groups\, each with their own unique style
  and personality\, but sharing the same passion for dance.\n\nImpakt is an
  all-inclusive group. Our aim is to build confidence\, create friendships\
 , and give every dancer the opportunity to shine.\n\nDivas and Dudes Perfo
 rmance Team is a small and energetic group of dancers who love to perform\
 , have fun\, and express themselves through a variety of dance styles.\n\n
 Together We Dance is a celebration of what can happen when we come togethe
 r\, support one another\, and simply enjoy the magic of dance.\n\nCelebrat
 ing Every Dancer. Every Ability. Every Dream.
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/im
 pakt-2.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1100@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20270203T164500
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20270203T164500
DTSTAMP:20260825T000342Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/rbo-gotterdammerung/
SUMMARY:ROYAL BALLET & OPERA: GÖTTERDÄMMERUNG
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: £15.50\, Film Society members/Regal Theatre Friends 
 £14.00\, Students/ES40s £13\, under 14s £10.\n\nPlease note start time\
 n\nThe Royal Opera LIVE from the Royal Opera House\n\nGÖTTERDÄMMERUNG [N
 ew Production]\n\nAn earth in ruin. The twilight of the Gods.\n\nDeception
  leads to treachery\, then devastation\, when Siegfried is tricked into be
 traying Brünnhilde.\n\nLearning the truth of her beloved’s innocence\, 
 Brünnhilde at last returns the ring to the Rhinemaidens\, before ordering
  that Valhalla be swallowed in flames.  For the long-awaited finale of Wa
 gner’s epic saga\, director Barrie Kosky situates the rich apocalyptic d
 rama in a contemporary world of dream-like turmoil.\n\nAntonio Pappano\, C
 onductor Laureate of The Royal Opera\, returns to take on the impassioned\
 , otherworldly music – including Siegfried’s transporting Funeral Marc
 h and Brünnhilde’s electrifying Immolation Scene.  The brilliant cast 
 is led by Elisabet Strid\, Andreas Schager and Mika Kares\, who together w
 ith the full forces of the Orchestra of the Royal Opera House and the Roya
 l Opera Chorus bring opera’s greatest journey to its shattering end.\n\n
 Sung in German with English subtitles.\n\nApproximate runtime 350min\, inc
 luding two Intervals
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/RB
 OGotterdammerung03.02.27-copy.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1092@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20270209T193000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20270209T193000
DTSTAMP:20260811T192524Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/exhibition-on-screen-renoir-and-love/
SUMMARY:EXHIBITION ON SCREEN: RENOIR AND LOVE
DESCRIPTION:ALL TICKETS £12\nExhibition on Screen – Renoir and Love\nDir
 ected by Ali Ray          90 mins\nPierre-Auguste Renoir is one o
 f the world's favourite artists.  A founding member of the Impressionist
  movement and a constantly evolving artist\, he is unmatched at depicting 
 human connection.  The National Gallery's blockbuster exhibition brings 
 together vibrant masterpieces which explore love in all its forms\, bringi
 ng colour and warmth into the cold winter months. \nWith exclusive access
  to this exciting new show\, Exhibition on Screen will bring these world c
 lass works to cinema audiences\, with close examination of the art and lea
 ding experts exploring the immense skill and influence of this master of c
 olour and connection.  Be transported back to a Parisian summer of love 
 through the eyes of a true visionary.  An unmissable opportunity to fall
  in love with Renoir this winter.\nMade in close collaboration with The Na
 tional Gallery\, London and Musee d'Orsay\, Paris.\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/EO
 SRenoirandLove09.02.27.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1115@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20270218T140000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20270220T190000
DTSTAMP:20260912T201240Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/trolls-jr-the-musical-2/
SUMMARY:TROLLS JR THE MUSICAL
DESCRIPTION:Ticket prices: Adult£10\, Child£6\, Family of 4 £25\n18th F
 ebruary- 20th\, February- 7:00 PM\n\nMatinee Saturday\, 20th- 2:00 PM\n\nT
 rolls JR. is based on the irreverent DreamWorks Animation movie franchise 
 and features a colourful\, wondrous world populated by hilariously unforge
 ttable characters. The show follows the overly optimistic Trolls\, constan
 tly with a song on their lips\, and the comically pessimistic Bergens\, wh
 o are only happy when they have Trolls in their stomachs.\n\nThe Troll the
 spians in Poppy’s company live by their motto: the show must go on. But 
 when a tyrannical foreign emissary arrives in Bergenland\, expectations ar
 e raised\, forcing the Trolls to totally rework their show or risk being s
 erved up in the name of diplomacy by a Chef rehired and out for revenge.\n
 \n&nbsp\;\n\n&nbsp\;
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/Tr
 olls-jr.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1101@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20270223T184500
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20270223T184500
DTSTAMP:20260825T000445Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/rbo-cosi-fan-tutte/
SUMMARY:ROYAL BALLET & OPERA: COSÌ FAN TUTTE
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: £15.50\, Film Society members/Regal Theatre Friends 
 £14.00\, Students/ES40s £13\, under 14s £10.\n\nPlease note start time\
 n\nThe Royal Opera LIVE from the Royal Opera House\n\nCOSÌ FAN TUTTE [New
  Production]\n\nSpurred on by a bet\, two young men hatch a plan to test t
 he fidelity of their girlfriends.  What follows is a slippery game of sed
 uction and power\, the four lovers plunging into a dizzying world of shift
 ing reality\, where truth becomes increasingly unstable.\n\nCosì fan tutt
 e has lost none of its sting since it first scandalised audiences in 1790.
   In her Main Stage debut\, Netia Jones\, Associate Director of The Royal
  Opera\, reimagines Mozart’s comedy of manners through a sharp contempor
 ary lens\, where 18th-century romantic trickery meets deeply satirical hig
 h-tech deceit.  Taking on the roles of the lovers is an exciting young ca
 st led by Louise Alder\, Simone McIntosh\, Mingjie Lei and Huw Montague Re
 ndall\, with Gerald Finley as their manipulative game-master Don Alfonso a
 nd Emily Pogorelc as Despina.  Thomas Hengelbrock conducts\, bringing out
  the exquisite melodies that underpin the provocative\, and resolutely mod
 ern\, themes at the heart of the opera.\n\nSung in Italian with English su
 btitles.\n\nApproximate runtime 210min\, including one Interval
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/RB
 OCosiFanTutte23.02.27-copy.jpeg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1102@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20270323T191500
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20270323T191500
DTSTAMP:20260825T000432Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/rbo-alices-adventures-in-wonderland/
SUMMARY:ROYAL BALLET & OPERA: ALICE'S ADVENTURES IN WONDERLAND
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: £15.50\, Film Society members/Regal Theatre Friends 
 £14.00\, Students/ES40s £13\, under 14s £10.\n\nPlease note start time\
 n\nThe Royal Ballet AS LIVE from the Royal Opera House\n\nALICE’S ADVENT
 URES IN WONDERLAND [Revival]\n\nFilmed 15th October 2024\n\nAt a garden pa
 rty on a sunny afternoon\, Alice is surprised to see her parents’ friend
  Lewis Carroll transform into a white rabbit.  When she follows him down 
 a rabbit hole\, events become curiouser and curiouser…  As Alice journe
 ys through Wonderland\, she encounters countless strange creatures. She’
 s swept off her feet by the charming Knave of Hearts\, who’s on the run 
 for stealing the tarts. Confusion piles upon confusion.  Then Alice wakes
  with a start.  Was it all a daydream?\n\nChristopher Wheeldon’s Alice
 ’s Adventures in Wonderland burst onto the stage in 2011 in an explosion
  of colour\, stage magic and inventive\, sophisticated choreography.  Job
 y Talbot’s score combines contemporary sound worlds with sweeping melodi
 es that gesture to ballet scores of the 19th century.  Bob Crowley’s wi
 ldly imaginative\, eye-popping designs draw on everything from puppetry to
  projections to make Wonderland wonderfully real.  The result shows The R
 oyal Ballet at its best\, bringing together world-class dance with enchant
 ing family entertainment and ingenious music and design.\n\nApproximate ru
 ntime 170min\, including two Intervals
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/RB
 OAlicesAdventuresInWonderland23.03.27.jpeg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1111@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20270327T193000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20270327T193000
DTSTAMP:20260828T202736Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/country-superstars/
SUMMARY:COUNTRY SUPERSTARS
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: Adult: £25.00/ Regal Friends\, Student\, ES40: £23.0
 0.\n&nbsp\;\n\nEach artist not only looks and sounds like the country star
  they portray\, these professional performers transform themselves through
  hours of practice at their craft. Every detail is taken into consideratio
 n\, from script\, choice of songs\, hair\, make-up\, and mannerisms\, as w
 ell as professional costumes and props. Kenny Rogers himself named and sta
 ted on his website that Sarah Jayne and Andy Crust's Tribute to Kenny and 
 Dolly is Europe's Leading Tribute Act. Country music will live on forever\
 , a must see for any fans of Country Music!\n\n&nbsp\;
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/Co
 untry-Superstars.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1103@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20270425T140000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20270425T140000
DTSTAMP:20260825T000420Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/rbo-swan-lake/
SUMMARY:ROYAL BALLET & OPERA: SWAN LAKE
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: £15.50\, Film Society members/Regal Theatre Friends 
 £14.00\, Students/ES40s £13\, under 14s £10.\n\nPlease note start time\
 n\nThe Royal Ballet ENCORE LIVE BROADCAST from the Royal Opera House\n\nSW
 AN LAKE [Revival]\n\nPrincess Odette is bound by a curse\, turned into a s
 wan by the evil sorcerer Von Rothbart.  The spell can only be broken by a
  pledge of eternal love.  When she meets Prince Siegfried\, he is immedia
 tely enamoured by her fragile beauty and pledges to free her.  But freedo
 m is not promised for Odette as Von Rothbart conspires to thwart the lover
 s’ plans.\n\nLiam Scarlett’s production for The Royal Ballet brings to
 gether Tchaikovsky’s towering score and John Macfarlane’s picturesque 
 designs to create an enduring ballet spectacle of love\, treachery and for
 giveness.\n\nApproximate runtime 205min\, including two Intervals 
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/RB
 OSwanLake25.04.27-copy.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1104@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20270505T190000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20270505T190000
DTSTAMP:20260825T000511Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/rbo-tosca/
SUMMARY:ROYAL BALLET & OPERA: TOSCA
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: £15.50\, Film Society members/Regal Theatre Friends 
 £14.00\, Students/ES40s £13\, under 14s £10.\n\nPlease note start time\
 n\nThe Royal Opera LIVE rom the Royal Opera House\n\nTOSCA [Revival]\n\nF
 loria Tosca and Mario Cavaradossi live for each other and for their art. 
  But when Cavaradossi helps an escaped prisoner\, the lovers make a deadl
 y enemy in the form of Baron Scarpia\, Chief of Police.  At the mercy of 
 Scarpia’s twisted desires\, Tosca is forced to make a horrific bargain: 
 sleeping with the man she hates\, in order to save the man she loves.  Ca
 n she find a way out?\n\nOliver Mears’s acclaimed production returns\, s
 etting Puccini’s operatic thriller in a contemporary\, war-torn Rome.  
 Daniel Oren conducts Aleksandra Kurzak\, who returns to the title role\, j
 oined by Saimir Pirgu as Cavaradossi and Christopher Maltman as Baron Scar
 pia.\n\nSung in Italian with English subtitles.\n\nApproximate runtime 195
 min\, including two Intervals
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/RB
 OTosca05.05.27-copy.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1093@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20270511T193000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20270511T193000
DTSTAMP:20260811T192456Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/exhibition-on-screen-monet/
SUMMARY:EXHIBITION ON SCREEN: MONET
DESCRIPTION:ALL TICKETS £12\nExhibition on Screen – Monet\nTo celebrate 
 Tate Britain's blockbuster Monet and Time exhibition\, Exhibition on Scr
 een is delighted to bring the iconic story of Claude Monet to cinema scree
 ns in May 2027. \nMonet was undeniably one of the world's favourite artis
 ts and the figurehead of the Impressionist movement.  Prepare to be dazz
 led by his spectacular and revolutionary use of light and colour and step 
 into one the most famous gardens in art history.  Immerse yourself in ic
 onic masterpieces and discover the incredible story of passion and rebelli
 on in this exciting documentary on the man who named the world's favourite
  art movement.
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/EO
 SMonet11.05.27.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1105@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20270525T191500
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20270525T191500
DTSTAMP:20260825T000524Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/rbo-romeo-and-juliet/
SUMMARY:ROYAL BALLET & OPERA: ROMEO AND JULIET
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: £15.50\, Film Society members/Regal Theatre Friends 
 £14.00\, Students/ES40s £13\, under 14s £10.\n\nPlease note start time\
 n\nThe Royal Ballet AS LIVE from the Royal Opera House\n\nROMEO AND JULIET
  [Revival]\n\nFilmed 20th March 2025\n\nThe Capulets and Montagues are swo
 rn enemies.  Yet it is love at first sight for Romeo Montague and Juliet 
 Capulet when they meet each other at the Capulet ball\, into which Romeo h
 as secretly gate-crashed.  The two fall in love and they profess their de
 votion to each other at Juliet’s balcony.  They secretly get married.\n
 \nThe stakes are raised for the young couple when Romeo avenges the death 
 of his friend Mercutio who has been killed by Tybalt\, Juliet’s cousin. 
  For this\, Romeo is exiled from Verona.  Meanwhile\, Juliet’s parents
  are forcing her to marry another suitor.  In order to be together\, Rome
 o and Juliet must risk it all.\n\nApproximate runtime 170min\, including t
 wo Intervals
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/RB
 ORomeoAndJuliet25.05.27-copy.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1118@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20270529T193000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20270529T193000
DTSTAMP:20260912T201055Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/oasiz-uk-tour-2027/
SUMMARY:OASIZ UK TOUR 2027
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: Early Bird offer - Adult: £12.00 for first 100 ticket
 s sold\, then increasing to Adult: £15.00\, Regal Friend /Student/ES40 £
 13.50.\nOASIZ are one of the UK’s most authentic tribute bands\, a point
  proved in 2023 when a short clip of frontman Steve performing as Liam wen
 t viral on social media with over half a million views. Many fans were con
 vinced the clip was actually of Liam Gallagher himself\, which led to the 
 story being covered in the national press as well as a high-profile TV app
 earance later that year.\nOASIZ are embarking on their fourth UK tour\, an
 d this is your chance to see them in top form. The setlist will include al
 l the greatest hits.\n\n&nbsp\;
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/oa
 siz-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1110@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20270604T193000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20270604T193000
DTSTAMP:20260828T202515Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/hannay-stands-fast/
SUMMARY:HANNAY STANDS FAST
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: Adults: £18/ Regal Friends and concessions: £16\n\nA
  thrilling sequel to “The 39 Steps”\, Hannay Stands Fast sees our dash
 ing hero\, Richard Hannay\, back in the fray on a mission to thwart a new 
 and deadly threat to his beloved England. Engaged on this top-secret case 
 by MI5\, Hannay makes his way down to Cornwall to infiltrate a secretive o
 rganisation and learn their dastardly plans. Can he save the day to keep t
 he nation safe for another day?\n\nHannay Stands Fast\, like its predecess
 or\, is taken on by four actors playing dozens of characters – 53 to be 
 precise! Set in various locations created through quick and innovative use
 s of trunks\, crates\, suitcases\, ladders\, you name it! A rip-roaring co
 medy for the whole family to enjoy – another of John Buchan’s classic 
 Hannay stories re-told for the stage through laughs\, daring-do\, and utte
 r chaos!\n\n&nbsp\;\n\n&nbsp\;
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/Ha
 nnay-Stands-Fast.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1108@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20270612T193000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20270612T193000
DTSTAMP:20260828T183053Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/from-gold-to-rio-the-greatest-hits-of-
 spandau-ballet-and-duran-duran/
SUMMARY:FROM GOLD TO RIO: THE GREATEST HITS OF SPANDAU BALLET AND DURAN DUR
 AN
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: Adult: £24.00/ Regal Friend\, Student\, ES40: £21.50
 \n\n&nbsp\;\n\nThe most exciting show to hit theatre land in many years!\n
 \nCelebrating the greatest hits of Spandau Ballet &amp\; Duran Duran!\n\nF
 rom Gold to Rio will take you on a nostalgic journey back to the New Roman
 tic era\, which ruled the charts for over a decade.\n\nFor the very first 
 time\, the music from two of the UK's most iconic bands will be celebrated
  in one power-packed show!\n\nWith over 20 top 10 hits\, the show will fea
 ture 2 hours of non-stop classics\, including Gold\, Rio\, True\, The Refl
 ex\, Through the Barricades\, Save A Prayer\, Lifeline\, Girls on Film\, t
 o name a few\, guaranteed to leave the audience shouting for more!\n\nPerf
 ormed by a full live band with over 30 years of professional experience\, 
 this show features excellent vocals\, tight harmonies\, along with a power
 house rhythm section.\n\nLee James is widely recognised as the most authen
 tic performer to Tony Hadley\, playing across the UK and Europe. Lee has p
 erformed with Tony on various occasions\, including BBC's The One Show on 
 two occasions\, the most recent being on 8th June 2022 to surprise a lady 
 on their Big Thank You segment. Lee is endorsed as the official tribute to
  Spandau Ballet by Gary Kemp and Tony himself.\n\n&nbsp\;\n\n&nbsp\;\n\n&n
 bsp\;\n\n&nbsp\;
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/fr
 om-rio-to-gold-image-2.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1095@regaltheatre.co.uk
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20270827T193000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20270827T193000
DTSTAMP:20260825T000936Z
URL:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/show/king-of-pop/
SUMMARY:KING OF POP STARRING NAVI
DESCRIPTION:TICKETS: Adults £25\; Regal Friends/Student/ES40 £23.50\nKing
  of Pop is led by the world’s greatest Michael Jackson tribute artist\, 
 ‘Navi’\, with his incredible live band and dancers. Michael Jackson pe
 rsonally gave Navi a standing ovation after he was invited to perform at o
 ne of his birthday parties.\n\nDue to Navi’s incredible resemblance to J
 ackson\, he was also hired as his official body double and decoy. Navi’s
  thrilling show will take you closer than ever imagined to an original Jac
 kson concert. Don’t miss this outstanding production featuring hits such
  as Smooth Criminal\, Beat It\, Billie Jean\, Black or White\, Man In The 
 Mirror and the ‘Jackson Five’ classics in a show suitable for the whol
 e family.\n\n&nbsp\;\n\n&nbsp\;
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://regaltheatre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/Ki
 ng_of_Pop_Nav.jpg
END:VEVENT
